course: dictionary
lesson: 10081
title: The theme of a story
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A theme is the big idea a text is really about. The plot is what happens; the theme is what it means. «Good wins over evil» and «be yourself» are themes, not events, so you can name a theme in a short phrase.
explain: To find a theme, ask what the story keeps coming back to. If a character learns to share, or the title is about courage, the theme is likely sharing or courage. A theme can also be the subject of a talk, a lesson or a party.
explain: Theme has more than one meaning, so the words around it help you choose. «A theme park posts its wait time, 45 minutes, so you can choose another ride» is about a park and its rides. «A theme song» is the music played with a show. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it fits.
explain: Phrases help too: the theme of, main theme, theme park, themed party. «Non-uniform or dress-up days usually raise money for charity, so you check the theme» means the style or idea chosen for that day.
fact: A theme is the main subject or idea of a talk, book, lesson, party or piece of art.
fact: A theme is also a big message a story is about, such as friendship, courage or kindness.
fact: «Themed» means decorated in one style, such as a space-themed week or a themed party.
fact: A theme tune or theme song is the music always played with a TV show or film.
fact: Theme is not the same as plot: the plot is what happens, and the theme is what it is really about.
exercise: «A theme park posts its wait time, 45 minutes, so you can choose another ride.» How long is the wait shown? | 5 hours | *45 minutes | 54 minutes | 4 minutes
exercise: In an English lesson, what is the theme of a story? | The number of pages | The plot, which is what happens | The name of the author | *A big message, such as friendship or courage
exercise: What is a theme tune? | A song about a park | A ticket to a theme park | *The music always played with a TV show or film | A lesson about themes
test: What does themed mean in a space-themed week? | Cancelled for the holidays | Split into two halves | *Decorated in one style, like space | Fast and loud
test: What is the main theme of a story? | The name of its main character | *The big idea it is really about, such as kindness | The number of chapters | Its title and cover
exam: Which word means the main subject or idea of a talk, book, lesson, party or piece of art? | *Theme | Plot | Chapter | Song
